subject: fix(db): normalize node:sqlite rows to plain objects for RSC serialization

node:sqlite (Node >= 22.5) returns rows with a null prototype. Next.js RSC
serialization rejects null-prototype objects when passed Server -> Client
("Only plain objects ... can be passed to Client Components"), causing the
Statistics page to 500 on deployments running Node 26 (mini2).

Normalize get()/all() results to plain objects so every consumer (repos,
RSC pages, API routes) sees the same shape as better-sqlite3 / sql.js rows.

Adds regression test asserting get/all return plain objects with enumerable
keys (verified: fails without fix, passes with fix).

